-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1, Subchapter IX -- LAYER 1, section 253:
-- the merger of a parent corporation and its subsidiary corporation or corporations.
--
-- The source is lines 1058 to 1171 of de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt, a plain-text rendering made by a converter script.
-- It is not the official text. `-- src:N | ...` is a slice of line N.
--
-- OUT OF RANGE (plain inputs, listed in NOTES.md): section 103 (dg1); section 251(g)(7)(A) and (B) (this piece: only whether the
-- certificate carries the provision); sections 252(d) and 258(c) (dg6 and dg7: which of them is "applicable"); section 262 (dg7:
-- the appraisal right itself); the laws of the other jurisdictions.
--
-- Section 253 does not say that the stockholders of the subsidiary vote: the mechanism it gives is the parent's board
-- resolution and the certificate of ownership and merger (NOTES.md, "What the text turns out to say").
-- COUNTS ARE VOTES (keel fork F5): "90% of the outstanding shares" is a proportion of shares, so section 212(a) makes it a
-- proportion of votes.

§ `s 253 -- merger of parent corporation and subsidiary corporation or corporations`

§§ `s 253(a) when the parent corporation may merge, and how`

-- One class of the subsidiary's stock: its votes, the votes the parent owns, and whether it has outstanding shares that, absent
-- this subsection, would be entitled to vote on the merger.
