-- The second condition of the first sentence, "(2) 1 or more of such corporations is a corporation of this State", unless the laws
-- of the foreign corporations' jurisdictions prohibit the merger. With the answer to the first condition (the 90% test), it
-- decides whether the parent may merge.
-- src:1137 | and (2) 1 or more of such corporations is a corporation of this State, unless the laws of the jurisdiction or jurisdictions under which the foreign corporation or corporations are organized prohibit such merger …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 253(a)(2) (src:1137)
GIVEN `the stock held satisfies s 253(a)(1)`                                                                                  IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the number of the parent and subsidiary corporations that are corporations of this State`                              IS A NUMBER
      `the laws of the jurisdiction under which a foreign corporation is organized prohibit the merger`                       IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: the laws of the other jurisdictions
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 253(a) the parent corporation may merge the subsidiary corporations under this section` `the stock held satisfies s 253(a)(1)` `the number of the parent and subsidiary corporations that are corporations of this State` `the laws of the jurisdiction under which a foreign corporation is organized prohibit the merger` MEANS
    IF    (`the number of the parent and subsidiary corporations that are corporations of this State` LESS THAN 1)
       OR `the laws of the jurisdiction under which a foreign corporation is organized prohibit the merger`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE `the stock held satisfies s 253(a)(1)`

-- How the parent may do it: merge the subsidiaries into itself and assume their obligations, or merge itself (or itself and
-- other subsidiaries) into one subsidiary, "by executing, acknowledging and filing ... a certificate of such ownership and merger".
-- src:1137 | the parent corporation may either merge the subsidiary corporation or corporations into itself and assume all of its or their obligations, or merge itself, or itself and 1 or more of such other subsidiary corporations, into 1 of the subsidiary corporations by executing, acknowledging and filing, in accordance with § 103 of this title, a certificate of such ownership and merger setting forth a copy of the resolution of its board of directors to so merge and the date of the adoption …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 253(a) (src:1137)
DECLARE `s 253(a) Direction of the merger` IS ONE OF
    `the parent corporation merges the subsidiary corporation or corporations into itself and assumes all of its or their obligations`
    `the parent corporation merges itself, or itself and one or more of the other subsidiary corporations, into one of the subsidiary corporations`

-- The certificate of ownership and merger. If the parent is not the surviving corporation, it states that the parent's
-- stockholders approved the merger (parent a corporation of this State) or that the parent adopted it under its own law
-- (parent a foreign corporation).
-- src:1137 | a certificate of such ownership and merger setting forth a copy of the resolution of its board of directors to so merge and the date of the adoption …
-- src:1137 | and the certificate of ownership and merger shall state that the proposed merger has been approved by a majority of the outstanding stock of the parent corporation entitled to vote thereon at a meeting duly called and held after 20 days’ notice of the purpose of the meeting given to each such stockholder at the stockholder’s address as it appears on the records of the corporation if the parent corporation is a corporation of this State or state that the proposed merger has been adopted, approved, certified, executed and acknowledged by the parent corporation in accordance with the laws under which it is organized if the parent corporation is a foreign corporation. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 253(a) (src:1137)
DECLARE `s 253(a) Certificate of ownership and merger` HAS
    `executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with s 103`                                    IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 103 (piece dg1)
    `sets forth a copy of the resolution of the board of directors of the parent corporation to merge` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sets forth the date of the adoption of the resolution`                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `states that the proposed merger has been approved by a majority of the outstanding stock of the parent corporation entitled to vote thereon at a meeting duly called and held after 20 days' notice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `states that the proposed merger has been adopted, approved, certified, executed and acknowledged by the parent corporation in accordance with the laws under which it is organized` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1137 | a certificate of such ownership and merger setting forth a copy of the resolution of its board of directors to so merge and the date of the adoption …
