-- The sentence defining "facts" in section 253(a): the same words as in section 251(b), read the same way (NOTES.md fork register F26): an
-- event, or a determination or action by any person or body (the corporation too), is a fact; anything else, the text does not say.
-- src:1137 | The term “facts,” as used in the preceding sentence, includes, but is not limited to, the occurrence of any event, including a determination or action by any person or body, including the corporation. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 253(a) (src:1137)
GIVEN item IS A `s 251(b) Kind of item that a term may depend on`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 253(a) the item is a fact within the meaning of the sentence on the resolution` item MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `an event, as the facts sentence of s 251(b) reads`                                                         THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a determination or action by a person or body, including the corporation, as the facts sentence of s 251(b) reads` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `something else, which the facts sentence of s 251(b) neither names nor excludes`                          THEN NOTHING

-- Where the parent is not the surviving corporation and is a corporation of this State, a majority of its outstanding stock
-- entitled to vote approves the merger. NOTHING (not covered) for a nonstock parent that does not survive (section 253(e) applies
-- the section to a nonstock parent only if it survives) and for counts that cannot be a vote.
