-- If the surviving corporation is a foreign corporation: (1) section 252(d) or section 258(c), as applicable, also applies;
-- (2) the terms and conditions of the merger obligate the surviving corporation to provide the agreement, and take the actions,
-- that section requires. Which of 252(d) and 258(c) is "applicable" is a legal conclusion drawn from sections 252 and 258
-- (dg6, dg7); here it is a plain input (NOTES.md fork register F14).
-- src:1137 | If the surviving corporation is a foreign corporation:
-- src:1138 | (1) Section 252(d) of this title or § 258(c) of this title, as applicable, shall also apply to a merger under this section; and
@ref 8 Del. C. § 253(a)(1) (src:1137-1138)
DECLARE `s 253(a)(1) Section that applies to a foreign surviving corporation` IS ONE OF
    `section 252(d)`
    `section 258(c)`

-- src:1137 | If the surviving corporation is a foreign corporation:
-- src:1138 | (1) Section 252(d) of this title or § 258(c) of this title, as applicable, shall also apply to a merger under this section; and
@ref 8 Del. C. § 253(a)(1) (src:1137-1138)
GIVEN `the surviving corporation is a foreign corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 258 and not section 252 is the applicable section` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: sections 252 (this piece) and 258 (piece dg7)
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 253(a)(1) Section that applies to a foreign surviving corporation`
`s 253(a)(1) the section that also applies to the merger` `the surviving corporation is a foreign corporation` `section 258 and not section 252 is the applicable section` MEANS
    IF NOT `the surviving corporation is a foreign corporation`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `section 258 and not section 252 is the applicable section`
         THEN JUST `section 258(c)`
         ELSE JUST `section 252(d)`

-- src:1137 | If the surviving corporation is a foreign corporation:
