GIVEN `the surviving corporation is a foreign corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the terms and conditions of the merger obligate the surviving corporation to provide the agreement, and take the actions, required by s 252(d) or s 258(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 253(a)(2) the terms of the merger must obligate the surviving corporation` `the surviving corporation is a foreign corporation` `the terms and conditions of the merger obligate the surviving corporation to provide the agreement, and take the actions, required by s 252(d) or s 258(c)` MEANS
        (NOT `the surviving corporation is a foreign corporation`)
    OR `the terms and conditions of the merger obligate the surviving corporation to provide the agreement, and take the actions, required by s 252(d) or s 258(c)`

§§ `s 253(b) a change of name`

-- A surviving Delaware corporation "may change its corporate name by the inclusion of a provision to that effect in the
-- resolution of merger adopted by the directors of the parent corporation and set forth in the certificate of ownership and
-- merger, and upon the effective date of the merger, the name of the corporation shall be so changed."
-- src:1140 | (b) If the surviving corporation is a Delaware corporation, it may change its corporate name by the inclusion of a provision to that effect in the resolution of merger adopted by the directors of the parent corporation and set forth in the certificate of ownership and merger, and upon the effective date of the merger, the name of the corporation shall be so changed.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 253(b) (src:1140)
GIVEN `the surviving corporation is a Delaware corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution adopted by the directors of the parent corporation includes a provision changing the corporate name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is set forth in the certificate of ownership and merger` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 253(b) the surviving corporation may change its corporate name` `the surviving corporation is a Delaware corporation` `the resolution adopted by the directors of the parent corporation includes a provision changing the corporate name` `the provision is set forth in the certificate of ownership and merger` MEANS
        `the surviving corporation is a Delaware corporation`
    AND `the resolution adopted by the directors of the parent corporation includes a provision changing the corporate name`
    AND `the provision is set forth in the certificate of ownership and merger`

-- src:1140 | (b) If the surviving corporation is a Delaware corporation, it may change its corporate name by the inclusion of a provision to that effect in the resolution of merger adopted by the directors of the parent corporation and set forth in the certificate of ownership and merger, and upon the effective date of the merger, the name of the corporation shall be so changed.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 253(b) (src:1140)
GIVEN `the corporation may change its corporate name under s 253(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the effective date of the merger has arrived`               IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: when it takes effect is section 103 (piece dg1)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 253(b) the name of the surviving corporation is changed` `the corporation may change its corporate name under s 253(b)` `the effective date of the merger has arrived` MEANS
        `the corporation may change its corporate name under s 253(b)`
    AND `the effective date of the merger has arrived`

§§ `s 253(c) other sections, and appraisal rights`

-- "Section 251(d) shall apply to a merger under this section, and section 251(e) shall apply to a merger under this section in
-- which the surviving corporation is the subsidiary corporation and is a corporation of this State."
