DECLARE `s 253(c) What s 251(d) and (e) call the agreement of merger` IS ONE OF
    `the resolution of merger adopted by the board of directors of the parent corporation`

-- src:1141 | References to “agreement of merger” in § 251(d) and (e) of this title shall mean for purposes of this subsection the resolution of merger adopted by the board of directors of the parent corporation. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 253(c) (src:1141)
`s 253(c) the document that s 251(d) and (e) call the agreement of merger` MEANS
    `the resolution of merger adopted by the board of directors of the parent corporation`

-- src:1141 | Any merger which effects any changes other than those authorized by this section or made applicable by this subsection shall be accomplished under § 251, § 252, § 257, or § 258 of this title. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 253(c) (src:1141)
GIVEN `the merger effects changes other than those authorized by s 253 or made applicable by s 253(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 253(c) the merger must be accomplished under s 251, s 252, s 257 or s 258` `the merger effects changes other than those authorized by s 253 or made applicable by s 253(c)` MEANS
    `the merger effects changes other than those authorized by s 253 or made applicable by s 253(c)`

-- "Section 262 of this title shall not apply to any merger effected under this section, except as provided in subsection (d)":
-- section 262 applies to the merger exactly when subsection (d) gives appraisal rights.
-- src:1141 | Section 262 of this title shall not apply to any merger effected under this section, except as provided in subsection (d) of this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 253(c) (src:1141)
GIVEN `the subsidiary is a corporation of this State party to the merger` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all of the stock of the subsidiary is owned by the parent corporation immediately prior to the merger` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 253(c) s 262 applies to the merger` `the subsidiary is a corporation of this State party to the merger` `all of the stock of the subsidiary is owned by the parent corporation immediately prior to the merger` MEANS
    `s 253(d) the stockholders of the subsidiary have appraisal rights as set forth in s 262` `the subsidiary is a corporation of this State party to the merger` `all of the stock of the subsidiary is owned by the parent corporation immediately prior to the merger`

§§ `s 253(d) appraisal rights`

-- "In the event all of the stock of a subsidiary Delaware corporation party to a merger effected under this section is not owned by
-- the parent corporation immediately prior to the merger, the stockholders of the subsidiary Delaware corporation party to the
-- merger shall have appraisal rights as set forth in section 262." The right is "as set forth in" section 262 (dg7): what the
-- stockholder must do to claim it is that section's.
-- src:1142 | (d) In the event all of the stock of a subsidiary Delaware corporation party to a merger effected under this section is not owned by the parent corporation immediately prior to the merger, the stockholders of the subsidiary Delaware corporation party to the merger shall have appraisal rights as set forth in § 262 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 253(d) (src:1142)
GIVEN `the subsidiary is a corporation of this State party to the merger` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all of the stock of the subsidiary is owned by the parent corporation immediately prior to the merger` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 253(d) the stockholders of the subsidiary have appraisal rights as set forth in s 262` `the subsidiary is a corporation of this State party to the merger` `all of the stock of the subsidiary is owned by the parent corporation immediately prior to the merger` MEANS
        `the subsidiary is a corporation of this State party to the merger`
    AND (NOT `all of the stock of the subsidiary is owned by the parent corporation immediately prior to the merger`)

§§ `s 253(e) nonstock corporations`

-- "This section shall apply to nonstock corporations if the parent corporation is such a corporation and is the surviving
-- corporation of the merger; ... references to the directors of the parent corporation shall be deemed to be references to
-- members of the governing body of the parent corporation, and references to the board of directors of the parent corporation
-- shall be deemed to be references to the governing body of the parent corporation."
-- src:1143 | (e) This section shall apply to nonstock corporations if the parent corporation is such a corporation and is the surviving corporation of the merger; provided, however, that references to the directors of the parent corporation shall be deemed to be references to members of the governing body of the parent corporation, and references to the board of directors of the parent corporation shall be deemed to be references to the governing body of the parent corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 253(e) (src:1143)
GIVEN kind                                                      IS A `Kind of corporation`
      `the parent corporation is the surviving corporation of the merger` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 253(e) this section applies to the nonstock corporation` kind `the parent corporation is the surviving corporation of the merger` MEANS
        `the kind is a nonstock corporation` kind
    AND `the parent corporation is the surviving corporation of the merger`

-- src:1143 | (e) This section shall apply to nonstock corporations if the parent corporation is such a corporation and is the surviving corporation of the merger; provided, however, that references to the directors of the parent corporation shall be deemed to be references to members of the governing body of the parent corporation, and references to the board of directors of the parent corporation shall be deemed to be references to the governing body of the parent corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 253(e) (src:1143)
GIVEN kind                                                      IS A `Kind of corporation`
      `the parent corporation is the surviving corporation of the merger` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 253(e) references to the parent corporation's directors and board are read as references to the members of its governing body and to its governing body` kind `the parent corporation is the surviving corporation of the merger` MEANS
    `s 253(e) this section applies to the nonstock corporation` kind `the parent corporation is the surviving corporation of the merger`

§§ `s 253(f) a charitable nonstock corporation`

-- "Nothing in this section shall be deemed to authorize the merger of a corporation with a charitable nonstock corporation, if
-- the charitable status of such charitable nonstock corporation would thereby be lost or impaired." Where it applies the section
-- does not authorize the merger (FALSE); where it does not, the subsection says nothing (NOTHING).
-- src:1144 | (f) Nothing in this section shall be deemed to authorize the merger of a corporation with a charitable nonstock corporation, if the charitable status of such charitable nonstock corporation would thereby be lost or impaired.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 253(f) (src:1144)
GIVEN kind                                                                  IS A `Kind of corporation`
      `the charitable status of the charitable nonstock corporation would be lost or impaired by the merger` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 253(f) this section authorizes the merger with the corporation` kind `the charitable status of the charitable nonstock corporation would be lost or impaired by the merger` MEANS
    IF    `the kind is a charitable nonstock corporation` kind
       AND `the charitable status of the charitable nonstock corporation would be lost or impaired by the merger`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING
